      "problem": "Factor the expression ${q}^{6}-27{d}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}-{b}^{3}=(a-b)({a}^{2}+ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a difference of cubes:\n\n$$\n{q}^{6}-27{d}^{3}={({q}^{2})}^{3}-{(3d)}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the given expression using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}^{6}-27{d}^{3} & ={({q}^{2})}^{3}-{(3d)}^{3} \\\\  & =({q}^{2}-3d)(({q}^{2})^{2}+{q}^{2}\\cdot 3d+(3d)^{2}) \\\\  & =({q}^{2}-3d)({q}^{4}+3d{q}^{2}+9{d}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
